          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Chern-Weil theory studies the refinement of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            and further to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
          %p
            The central operation that models this refinement is the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} Chern-Weil homomorphism
            from
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            by choosing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            and evaluating its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\nabla
            in the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -\rangle
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            to produce the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+characteristic+form"} curvature characteristic form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo ∇
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle F_\nabla \rangle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
          %p
            Concretely, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} Chern-Weil homomorphism
            is presented by the following construction:
          %p For
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo ∈
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G \in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
                of (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
                underlying) a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %li
              %p
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c] \in H^n(B G, \mathbb{Z})
                a class in its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
                – which we may call a
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class"} characteristic class
                for
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
          %p
            we get for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            an assignment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [c] : G Bund(X)_\sim \to H^n(X,\mathbb{Z})
          %p
            on integral cohomology classes of base space to equivalence classes of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to B G
            to the class
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f^* c]
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi c
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c]_\mathbb{R} \in H^n(B G, \mathbb{R})
            be the image of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c]
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}
          %p
            The
            %strong first main statement
            of Chern-Weil theory is that there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi c
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle- \rangle :=  \phi^{-1} [c]_{\mathbb{R}}
          %p
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            associated to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi c
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c]_{\mathbb{R}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            (of real
            = succeed ")s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi inv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi
                  \\;\colon\;
                  inv(\mathfrak{g})
                  \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  H^\bullet(B G, \mathbb{R})
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %strong second main statement
            is that this invariant polynomial serves to provide a
            %em differential
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"}> Lie integration
            ) construction of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi c
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c]_{\mathbb{R}}
          %p
            for any choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            on a
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            we have the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            2-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\nabla \in \Omega^2(P, \mathfrak{g})
            and fed into the invariant polynomial this yields an
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\langle F_\nabla \wedge \cdots \wedge F_\nabla \rangle
                  \\in
                  \\Omega^n(X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The statement is that under the
            = succeed "-isomorphism" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi dR
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet_{dR}(X) \simeq H^\bullet(X, \mathbb{R})
            this presents the class
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi c
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c]_{\mathbb{R}}
          %p
            The
            = succeed "," do
              %strong third main statement
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle F_\nabla \wedge \cdots F_\nabla\rangle
            may be realized itself as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle n-bundle with connection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat \mathbf{c}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mi Bund
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi Bund
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi diff
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\hat \mathbf{c}] :
                  G Bund_\nabla(X)_\sim
                  \\to
                  U(1) n Bund_\nabla(X)_\sim
                  \\simeq H^n_{diff}(X)
                  \\,.
          %p In summary this yields the following picture:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mover
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mo ∇
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi ⋯
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mo ∇
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi c
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi H
                            %mi diff
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
